{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice","id":977718,"title":"\"Clockwork Mage\" build advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T06:11:29-07:00","id":977718,"title":"\"Clockwork Mage\" build advice","content":"There's some cool clockpunk stuff in Awakening, and I love the aesthetic, so I'm wondering what the best way would be to build a Mage who specializes in creating clockwork devices and clockwork-themed magic. <br /> <br /> To put it another way, how would I make a Mechanomancer in Awakening, ideally including the gradual destruction of the self and ever-increasing inability to function in the modern world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:27:19-07:00","id":977726,"title":"","content":"Austere or similar legacy plus heavy use of Matter, a clockwork shadow name, and relevant Yantras. An Obsession with Ashir Arif (Spelling?) and/or the Schaefer Movement wouldn't hurt either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-28-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:55:16-07:00","id":977912,"title":"","content":"Also, dots in Crafts with a relevant Specialty, and Rotes using Crafts as a Mudra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:26:00-07:00","id":978215,"title":"","content":"Hm, I found it a bit odd that Night Horrors Clockwork Man I Can't Spell His Name was a mastigos, since Obrimos, Moros, and even Acanthus all seem like better fits. Ah well, I'm all for path flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:58:04-07:00","id":978402,"title":"","content":"paths are meant to be sufficiently flexible so that with varying amounts of effort, they can accommodate nearly every concept that doesn't require an array of <i>specific</i> spells or arcana to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:31:30-07:00","id":979954,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I get that, I was just commenting that Mastigos wouldn't even be my third choice for a master of clockwork. <br /> <br /> I don't even think I need to homebrew anything with the No Path or Yantra Reliance hacks to get what I'm looking for here, since while this is sort of a &quot;mad scientist&quot; thing I feel like magic clockwork is significantly fantastical that it works better with the aesthetics of the Awakened than it would as something a minor template mad scientist or GM cultist would make. <br /> <br /> A bonus is that unlike in UA it's relatively easy for a Mage to make clockwork prosthetics and so on, while there the book explicitly says you need an Epideromancer helping to make it work. <br /> <br /> Though, some really punishing homebrew restrictions could be nice to get the &quot;Higher Tier Mechanomancer&quot; feel, what with the whole inevitable self destruction angle. I especially love how Mechanomancers power their machines by sacrificing their own memories, is there any way I could do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:18:02-07:00","id":980032,"title":"","content":"Well, &quot;clockwork mage&quot; is a pretty broad aesthetic. A clockwork mastigos would, because of their ruling arcana, focus on mind and space magic that treated people-as-gears/interchangeable parts.<br /> <br /> What you're describing as what you want is pretty much a textbook member of the Austere legacy from the Guardians of the Veil book. All you'd have to do is update it to 2e. Outside of that or a similar Legacy, I don't think you can do what you want unless you enchant mundane prosthetic with various spells and effects, then wear them like normal people do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:34:02-07:00","id":980037,"title":"","content":"Really? Wouldn't it just be Matter+Life or even just Matter to make a working clockwork prosthetic?<br /> <br /> I always thought it was ridiculous that The Unbidden treated relatively simple clockwork automatons as wondrous marvels that no modern mages could duplicate. The little piece of fiction where one of the characters goes &quot;I know we're literal wizards who can control the fabric of the universe...but a robot? That's ridiculous!&quot; doesn't help either. Are you honestly telling me that it isn't trivial for mages to whip up a simple robot? Especially since the book that has the clockworks also has vastly more powerful artificial beings that were created by more recent Mages (Gnomon and the pseudo-Promethean)? And how Mechanomancers can make small armies of clockwork servants, despite being orders of magnitude less powerful than Awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:53:43-07:00","id":980044,"title":"","content":"if you know enough Matter to animate an object, or enough Matter and Life to imbue it with life, there's nothing stopping you from animating a little golem using robot parts. It's no more trivial for a mage to &quot;whip up&quot; a robot than it is for any sleeper. The mage can supplement a home made robot with some spells, but short of just making it a golem and doing all of it with magic, magic isn't much of a shortcut.<br /> <br /> What spell would you use to create a clockwork arm?<br /> <br /> The quote mentioned is an example of someone complaining that robots are largely out of genre for the setting. It's a game of modern sorcery, not an episode of Doctor Who.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:02:16-07:00","id":980048,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Matter and Life are enough to crank out a small army of robots. The implication that no one has duplicated or surpassed Clockwork Guy's inventions just doesn't make sense. <br /> <br /> Like I said, Matter and Life or just Matter. <br /> <br /> Greek mythology had magical automatons. So did The Faerie Queene. Mad science ended up pretty much replacing sorcery in the popular consciousness and in horror media. A modern sorcery setting where the characters are surprised to see clockwork robots isn't any sort of modern sorcery setting I can endorse. Robots and mad scientists are more important to modern horror than wizards and demons. Who narrates The Monster Mash? It ain't a wizard. <br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, take a shot every time someone on this forum mentions Doctor Who in relation to ChroD. Take two shots when someone specifically compares something in it to Mage. Say goodbye to your liver. It's not a good comparison to make, when DW is pretty influential to modern horror and weird fiction and a pretty big contingent of people see it as completely compatible with ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:10:36-07:00","id":980049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980037#post980037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought it was ridiculous that The Unbidden treated relatively simple clockwork automatons as wondrous marvels that no modern mages could duplicate. The little piece of fiction where one of the characters goes &quot;I know we're literal wizards who can control the fabric of the universe...but a robot? That's ridiculous!&quot; doesn't help either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that reading of the text is exceedingly uncharitable.<br /> <br /> I feel this because it is nonsensical when placed next to the actual content.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Autonomous Laboratory</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we never should have gone into that old ruin. Edge and I both knew it was dangerous. Hell, over a beer, sitting just at the entrance we\u2019d found, we both agreed we should turn back and tell someone more important in the Order. We went in anyway.<br /> <br /> The place had all the traps and triggers you\u2019d expect, that wasn\u2019t anything new. Besides, Edge was good at puzzles. I was only really good at getting us into trouble. I heard the sound first. Sort of like a grandfather clock being dragged slowly over stone. The whirs and clicks the thing made gave it away a long time before we could see it. That didn\u2019t matter, since it already knew how to find us.<br /> <br /> <b>Edge said; \u201cJesus, it\u2019s some kind of robot!\u201d I told him he was being stupid when we both saw what looked like a little man made out of copper and brass.</b> And then something changed in that room. I don\u2019t know, it was something you\u2019d barely noticed, like a furnace kicking on. But that little copper fucker just lurched forward and ripped Edge\u2019s arm off like his bones were made of butter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most magical constructs you find in a ruin are going to more strongly resemble golems or monsters just by virtue of a lower threshold of complexity required for an ambulatory form when magic is involved. Most magical constructs you find in a ruin are also going to pre-date the <i>word</i> &quot;robot,&quot; never mind the modern conception of the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:12:41-07:00","id":980051,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://m.memegen.com/e9y43p.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Congrats on missing my point and getting the last word","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:15:29-07:00","id":980053,"title":"","content":"Ah, the good ol' &quot;I won't tell you what my point was, but ya sure missed it!&quot;. I need to use that one more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:17:31-07:00","id":980057,"title":"","content":"On a constructive note, I'm thinking Silver Ladder or Mysterium as her Order. Since she's based on UA's Mechanomancy, I'd say she's a Mage who subscribes to the &quot;revive the ancient atlantean utopia&quot; agenda, since Mechanomancers are based partially on the concept of &quot;reviving the future we were promised but didn't get&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still looking for a way for her to sacrifice her memories to power her machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:26:07-07:00","id":980063,"title":"","content":"the point is that if you use magic to do all the work of making a pile of inert matter function, it's a <i>golem</i>. making actual robots that are functional and not just glorified RC cars is really expensive and difficult and complicated. The more you throw magic at the problem, the less a robot the end result is and the more it is a golem with hinges.<br /> <br /> the point was that your complaint about a quote took the quote out of context to imply something it didn't mean. Then when I tried to explain it, you couldn't get off your high horse and instead turned it into &quot;oh no the mean ChroD players don't like my thing I like, but they're so ignorant that they don't understand that it totally fits in my idealized game&quot; thing that you do every time.<br /> <br /> You seem to literally want to hot glue gears onto mage and call it mad science. Good for you. I'd say that I've learned not to engage with you anymore, but only time will tell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:37:42-07:00","id":980070,"title":"","content":"And now it's you who're missing the point, but I'm going to explain it: mad science is literally just magic with gears glued on. That's what differentiates it from actual science. That's what I'm going for. I don't care that a magical automaton is &quot;technically&quot; a golem and not a real robot. That's what makes it horror and not hard scifi. And I didn't take the quote out of context, because you explained what you thought it meant, and I said that I was aware of that but thought it was a dumb thing for the book to imply. <br /> <br /> Oh No The Mean ChroD Player Used A Bad Analogy To Imply Something That Didn't Make Sense.<br /> <br /> You entered this thread by saying Mages wouldn't be able to easily create prosthetic limbs or automatons without using an Attainment which <br /> <br /> A. Isn't really supported by the rules. <br /> <br /> And <br /> <br /> B. Shouldn't be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:49:58-07:00","id":980078,"title":"","content":"Actually I entered into this thread saying that you can fit seemingly out of theme concepts into any path with a little flexibility and elbow grease. Then I said the thing that you want to do is supported by a legacy so you should look into that for inspiration. Then when that wasn't good enough, I asked you what spells you want to use to do what you want and you just kinda glossed over the point by saying &quot;spells&quot; and then going on to complain about the setting that isn't enough like the game you want the game to be.<br /> <br /> If we want to get <i>technical</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:50:14-07:00","id":980079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980070#post980070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now it's you who're missing the point, but I'm going to explain it: mad science is literally just magic with gears glued on. That's what differentiates it from actual science. That's what I'm going for. I don't care that a magical automaton is &quot;technically&quot; a golem and not a real robot. That's what makes it horror and not hard scifi. And I didn't take the quote out of context, because you explained what you thought it meant, and I said that I was aware of that but thought it was a dumb thing for the book to imply.<br /> <br /> Oh No The Mean ChroD Player Used A Bad Analogy To Imply Something That Didn't Make Sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably going to ignore this like most other questions thrown your way, but why do you even <i>care</i>? It seems that all you really want to do is make Mage into Genius or whatever, but why do you even <i>care</i>? Why not just play Genius? I've literally never seen you mention a single thing about Mage you like, so why even bother going through the trouble of turning something you've shown no indication of caring about whatsoever into a game that already exists that you seem to already enjoy playing? <br /> <br /> For the longest I've been trying to figure out your angle with all of this. I'm not sure if you're just trying to rock the boat for shits and giggles, or if you're actually serious about all of this. And giving you the benefit of the doubt and assuming you're actually serious, I just can't figure out why you even care. Do you just want a 2nd edition of Genius to play with? If so you'd have a much easier time getting the community to just do that instead of trying to make Mage into Genius 1.5.<br /> <br /> So lets cut the crap, what exactly are you trying to get out of this? Do you want to play Mage or are you trying to just use it as a substitute for what you're actually wanting to play? If what you're looking for is Genius 2.0 with mechanics as sleek as Mage just <i>say so</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:54:49-07:00","id":980081,"title":"","content":"I made a whole thread where I explained what I was going for. I want to hack Mage so that the problems I have with it aren't as pressing and I'm more able to enjoy all the content that's been made for it, since Genius is unlikely to ever have a finished second edition or magically become canon. And I do answer questions. People just keep asking them after I've answered them. <br /> <br /> What I'm trying to get out of this thread specifically is advice for how to build a Mage who focuses on creating clockwork devices. As far as I can tell, people got mad because I interpreted a part of Night Horrors: The Unbidden uncharitably. I've also been asking if there's any way to represent the mechanic in UA where Mechanomancers fuel their machines by sacrificing their own memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:02:14-07:00","id":980085,"title":"","content":"You want a mage that makes clockwork stuff? Give them a bunch of crafts dots and a specialty in clockwork. Make clockwork prosthetic and animate them with a ritual spell and pay the costs to make it permanent, then strap them to your self. Then spend an action every time you need to order the golem arm prosthetic to do something. It's resource intensive, but it's not exactly a complex series of actions.<br /> <br /> If you want to do more esoteric and weird things, then you need to figure it out and not expect other people to do the heavy lifting for you. It's your character,<i> you figure it out</i> and then post something along the lines of &quot;Hey I want to do (A, B, C) and so I think that I can do it by doing (X, Y, Z). What do you think?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:06:27-07:00","id":980088,"title":"","content":"Alright, so reading between the lines, you don't think Genius is going to get a 2nd edition so you want to try to convert the closest thing ChroD has into a good substitute. There we go, that's all you needed to say.<br /> <br /> Alright, now answer this question. What parts of Mage do you like and want to keep? Is it just the mechanics? Do you particularly care for any of the lore? If all you care about is mechanics it'd be easier to just excise the lore/setting completely and harvest the general mechanics and repurpose all of the things that need to be tinkered with to make the new setting fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:07:05-07:00","id":980089,"title":"","content":"Hm, I feel like it would be worth it to work out a refinement of the Arcana/casting system that makes it simpler to create gadgets/items that do things. And for the arm, couldn't I just build a clockwork arm with Crafts, use a Matter and Life spell to attach it, and just get an extra Brawl die and no penalty for fighting armed opponents unarmed because I have a metal arm?<br /> <br /> A question: what would be the difference between using Matter + Mind or using Matter + Life to animate something? Say I want to make a clockwork scorpion that can follow orders, which of those would be better?<br /> <br /> And that is exactly what I said in my Mage hack thread, yes. And here's a list of things I like about Mage, despite it not being related to the thread topic at all, because you requested it;<br /> <br /> - The Astral is cool. <br /> - The Seers are pretty interesting antagonists. <br /> - The overarching mythology is pretty interesting. <br /> - The paths can be restrictive, but they are fairly flavorful and interesting so I don't want to jettison them altogether. <br /> - The spellcasting system is probably as streamlined as possible. <br /> - Overall, I think Awakening is a pretty good urban fantasy/superhero game on its own, but that I need to change a few things if I want to play it as part of ChroD. <br /> <br /> And again, Mage isn't going to go away no matter what I do. I'm trying to change as little as possible for the sake of convenience. If I change too much, I'll have to go through any Mage books I want to use with a metaphorical red pen, stopping every five words to scribble in &quot;There are no more Paths so ignore this part&quot; and &quot;I replaced the Seers with the Lemurians so this part doesn't work&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:20:29-07:00","id":980101,"title":"","content":"Actually, it's pretty important because it helps get to the heart of the issue. Long story short, with the changes you seem to want to make you aren't going to be playing part of the ChroD regardless, so you might as well throw that idea out the window. You seem to want a lot of mechanical and setting changes that's going to mean you definitely aren't playing Mage anymore, but a homebrew game that is similar, but still a bit different than the base Mage game.<br /> <br /> As you've noted, Mage isn't going to go away, and it probably isn't ever going to cater to your Genius needs in the way your probably want it to. So we're going to need to hybrid this shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:39:22-07:00","id":980108,"title":"","content":"We should probably only be discussing this in terms of how it relates to the topic of this thread, but okay. I'm not sure how the changes would prevent me from playing part of ChroD, since one of their main purposes is to bring Mage more in line with the themes of the setting as a whole. <br /> <br /> The main goal for my mechanical and setting changes is to make it something where you could take an existing mage supplement, read it through, and find only a few contradictions that could be easily resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:52:45-07:00","id":980116,"title":"","content":"If you're going to change it to essentially be a Genius replacement I don't see why you wouldn't just go whole hog with it. Pretty much everything you've said or talked about indicates that you want to make it more and more like Genius, you might as well just take the plunge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:03:15-07:00","id":980120,"title":"","content":"Because, as I've mentioned, Onyx Path isn't going to start making Genius. Genius isn't played or discussed outside of a small subset of the fandom. There will be no Genius content in Dark Eras or The Crossover Chronicle. <br /> <br /> Here's a question for you: what is it about what I want that radically changes the essence of Mage? Because a lot of people have told me that what I'm looking for is already there. As an example, the MCG already includes rules for mad scientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:13:14-07:00","id":980122,"title":"","content":"If you're already aware of mad science variant rules for mage, why aren't those good enough?<br /> <br /> I'll tell you why. Because when people sit down to play Mage, they expect to play<i> Mage</i>. Not &quot;three mages and a that one character who claims he's just a mad scientist and wants to argue about the setting all the time.&quot; Using variant rules that turn &quot;Mage&quot; into &quot;Mad Scientist&quot; cuts out the player base that wants to play <i>Mage </i>and leaves you with people who largely scratch their itch by playing Genius or other games more suited to that genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:20:48-07:00","id":980126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980120#post980120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, as I've mentioned, Onyx Path isn't going to start making Genius. Genius isn't played or discussed outside of a small subset of the fandom. There will be no Genius content in Dark Eras or The Crossover Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Here's a question for you: what is it about what I want that radically changes the essence of Mage? Because a lot of people have told me that what I'm looking for is already there. As an example, the MCG already includes rules for mad scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be wanting mechanics that force a certain play style. They're right in that Mage does have pretty much all of the things you're looking for, but you really seem hung up on &quot;emphasizing&quot; those aspects, which I take to mean adding mechanics that force players to act a certain way or be penalized mechanically. Simply put, that isn't really what Mage is about. Does it have horror? Sure, but it isn't forced. You aren't a vampire or a werewolf. You don't randomly lose control over your character so that the ST can make you do 'bad things' so that your character can feel bad about themselves and cry woe is me. Pretty much everything you've posted screams that that is what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:34:41-07:00","id":980293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980120#post980120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, as I've mentioned, Onyx Path isn't going to start making Genius. Genius isn't played or discussed outside of a small subset of the fandom. There will be no Genius content in Dark Eras or The Crossover Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Here's a question for you: what is it about what I want that radically changes the essence of Mage? Because a lot of people have told me that what I'm looking for is already there. As an example, the MCG already includes rules for mad scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things come to mind:<br /> <br /> One, if you really want to run &quot;mad scientists&quot; then I wouldn't shy away from using a fangame like Genius (or writing one of your own, especially since you're building a rather substantial hack anyway).<br /> <br /> Two, if you're looking for hacks, especially Path hacks that might shake up play styles, then you might want to check out this old thread which has plenty of ideas: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...upernal-realms</a> (and there are tons more threads like this one in the depths of the Mage forums).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:16:33-07:00","id":980483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980126#post980126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be wanting mechanics that force a certain play style. They're right in that Mage does have pretty much all of the things you're looking for, but you really seem hung up on &quot;emphasizing&quot; those aspects, which I take to mean adding mechanics that force players to act a certain way or be penalized mechanically. Simply put, that isn't really what Mage is about. Does it have horror? Sure, but it isn't forced. You aren't a vampire or a werewolf. You don't randomly lose control over your character so that the ST can make you do 'bad things' so that your character can feel bad about themselves and cry woe is me. Pretty much everything you've posted screams that that is what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you consider the horror in vampire and werewolf to be &quot;forced&quot;? Then there's a quandary here, since I love both of those games, and how their mechanics and setting emphasize the monstrosity of the protagonists. That's what I think Mage should have done, and that's what I'm trying to do. I actually think Mage needs more of that than any of the other games, because it has farther to go to make the characters undeniably monstrous. Vampires, werewolves, etc are instantly recognizable as monsters, but mages don't have that immediate association with monstrosity. They're the most human splat, too, and I always disliked how the most human splat was the most powerful. To be honest, I think of the player base who wants to play Mage &quot;as written&quot; and pushed back against my suggestions the same way I think of the people who play vampions-style. There's nothing wrong with it per se, it's just not what I look for in ChroD. And to be honest, people who look at Mage and go &quot;this shouldn't have mad scientists in it&quot; are not people I have much interest in playing with or discussing things with, because we have very different perceptions of horror fiction and want very different things out of the game. I personally think that people who don't want mad science in Mage are wrong as objectively as it's possible to be wrong about something like this, and if I can persuade them, that's fine, but if I can't, well, they're welcome to it. <br /> <br /> Again, all of this is off topic from actual build advice.<br /> <br /> Again again, I still have no idea how substantial my hack is going to be, because half of you are saying what I want is already there and half of you are saying that I'm going for a radical departure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:50:22-07:00","id":980500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980483#post980483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you consider the horror in vampire and werewolf to be &quot;forced&quot;? Then there's a quandary here, since I love both of those games, and how their mechanics and setting emphasize the monstrosity of the protagonists. That's what I think Mage should have done, and that's what I'm trying to do. I actually think Mage needs more of that than any of the other games, because it has farther to go to make the characters undeniably monstrous. Vampires, werewolves, etc are instantly recognizable as monsters, but mages don't have that immediate association with monstrosity. They're the most human splat, too, and I always disliked how the most human splat was the most powerful. To be honest, I think of the player base who wants to play Mage &quot;as written&quot; and pushed back against my suggestions the same way I think of the people who play vampions-style. There's nothing wrong with it per se, it's just not what I look for in ChroD. And to be honest, people who look at Mage and go &quot;this shouldn't have mad scientists in it&quot; are not people I have much interest in playing with or discussing things with, because we have very different perceptions of horror fiction and want very different things out of the game. I personally think that people who don't want mad science in Mage are wrong as objectively as it's possible to be wrong about something like this, and if I can persuade them, that's fine, but if I can't, well, they're welcome to it.<br /> <br /> Again, all of this is off topic from actual build advice.<br /> <br /> Again again, I still have no idea how substantial my hack is going to be, because half of you are saying what I want is already there and half of you are saying that I'm going for a radical departure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it like this. I feel that pretty much any bad thing a vampire or werewolf does under the influence of such mechanics to be less monstrous than the same or similar acts done while not under their influence. Werewolves and vampires don't have a choice, and aren't completely responsible for their actions in those states. It's like being forced to take mind altering drugs by an outside source. You didn't choose to take the drugs, and aren't in control of the actions you commit while under their influence. Murdering someone in that state is, imo, less horrific than cold calculated murder maliciously planned out over some perceived grievance committed by whoever it is you're targeting. <br /> <br /> As for views on what does and doesn't fit in Mage, to be honest, officially, what you think doesn't really mean a thing. You are not, and have little to no influence over, the people who write and develop the game and decide what it is. So again, thinking they're wrong about something doesn't really mean squat. Now don't feel too bad about that because most people are in the exact same boat. Now at your table specifically, you have liberty to change things as much as you want, <b><i><u>but</u></i></b> even then you have to worry about your players willingness to accept such changes.<br /> <br /> And no, I really don't think anyone is really disagreeing that most (not going to say all without re-reviewing everything you've said first) of what you want is already there. It's what you want to do to force it that most people seem to be disagreeing with. It is currently there, but it isn't forced, which is how it is meant to be. No, there's nothing forcing it, but as you've been told many times, that's the point. If you want to emphasize these already present aspects without changing anything mechanically, or really even setting-wise, you need to do that on an ST level. Push those themes more to the forefront with how you present whatever story it is that you attempt to tell. Make sure your players are ready and willing to cater as heavily to the specific themes you want them to, and then just <i>play the game</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:14:27-07:00","id":980503,"title":"","content":"See, we disagree on the nature of &quot;forced&quot;. I don't think that having mechanics that emphasize the monstrosity of the protagonists. Unknown Armies has, in addition to the most detailed sanity meter of any tabletop game, restrictions and costs for each school of magic that pretty much force any practicioner of it to be, at the very least, weird and somewhat distanced from othera, and a barely functional raving madman at higher levels of power. I don't consider this bad game design or forcing. The themes of the game explicitly spell out that it's about broken people trying to change the world, and that magic will destroy you. Having mechanics that support these themes is not railroading or bad game design. It's the same as an action movie based rpg that rewards players for doing over the top stunts- it uses game mechanics to support its theme. Generic systems like GURPs are there if you don't want that, but ChroD is a system that's designed to tell a specific type of story, and each game system is meant to communicate the idea of monstrosity in some way. If I wanted a game about people with superpowers who could potentially do horrible things with them, I'd play any number of other RPGs. I play ChroD because I like exploring horror archetypes, not just having magic powers. <br /> <br /> Another thing: it's very easy to argue the opposite of what you're saying. Many people find stories in which the protagonists must fight to overcome their own flaws and condition to be very compelling. To turn your statement around, murdering someone under the influence of a supernatural power is less evil than planning it out...but resisting the urge to do evil even when there are forces pressing for you to give into it is more impressive than not doing evil when you have no real incentive for doing it. I prefer that ChroD protagonists be, on some level, broken people and monsters. Vampire wouldn't be anywhere near as interesting if there was no Beast and no need to drink blood, because then you'd just be a superhero. Someone on the forum actually has a signature that even says something like &quot;is it better to be born good or to overcome one's evil nature?&quot; or something like that. My preferences regarding Mage are things that I think the game should have done in the first place, for the reasons I've explained. If you like Mage completely as it is, I'm sorry, but I guess we just aren't going to see eye to eye. <br /> <br /> As I've said, I dislike the &quot;they're monsters because they could do bad things with their powers&quot; trope. You can disagree, but no matter how many times you repeat it it won't win me over. <br /> <br /> In a desperate attempt to get us back on topic, does the character concept I proposed go against the nature of the game or setting in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-03-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:38:55-07:00","id":980510,"title":"","content":"A Mage who is obsessed with clockwork is fine for the setting.<br /> <br /> You still haven't addressed the issue that these things you're looking for do in fact actually exist in the system but it's up to the ST to deliver the story that drives those themes home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:57:51-07:00","id":980516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980503#post980503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ChroD is a system that's designed to tell a specific type of story, and each game system is meant to communicate the idea of monstrosity in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me emphasize this real quick. This is a point the carries a lot of truth. You are correct, ChroD games are designed to tell certain types of stories, and each system is meant to communicate monstrosity in certain ways. Mage is no exception to this. It chooses the type of monstrosity that it wants to focus on, tells you up front what that is, and delivers upon that magnificently imo. That said, here's the disconnect that you are running into. <i>You don't like that type of monstrosity that mage is built upon exploring</i>. This isn't a fault of the game, this isn't a flaw. It has its premise, and its one you don't like. As such, almost everything based off of this premise is going to be something you don't like because you don't like the foundation that it's built upon. There's nothing wrong with Mage as is, you just don't like the idea behind the line.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you've been told what the premise and base of Mage is about enough times for me to need to remind you, but let me tell you straight up that Mage isn't Genius. <i>Mage will never be Genius</i>. They might have some similarities, but Mage is its own distinct beast. The game you're wanting to play is pretty obviously not Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing: it's very easy to argue the opposite of what you're saying. Many people find stories in which the protagonists must fight to overcome their own flaws and condition to be very compelling. To turn your statement around, murdering someone under the influence of a supernatural power is less evil than planning it out...but resisting the urge to do evil even when there are forces pressing for you to give into it is more impressive than not doing evil when you have no real incentive for doing it. </div> </div> </div>I never said it wasn't compelling. I said it wasn't as horrifying to me. What is and isn't compelling is a completely different topic. And you act like Mages aren't resisting the pressure to do bad things. That's what Mage is all about. The temptation to do bad things for greater gain. And that's one of the really important things about Mage, they are <i>tempted</i>. They aren't forced, they're <i>tempted.</i> It isn't a temptation if you have no choice about whether you have to do something or not.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I feel that Mage handles temptation to do wrong better than any other line in ChroD for a few very simple reasons. One, how <i>human</i> Mages are. They aren't like Demons, whose thought processes, morality, and everything else that makes them them is so completely different than your average joe. That makes them so much more relatable. You can intimately understand their wants, needs, and the temptations that they face. Another is that, as I've mentioned, they're actually <i>tempted</i>. They aren't forced to do one thing or another because the mechanics say they're mind controlled into having to do so. There's no, you black out and do all the bad things I tried to tempt you into doing. No, they have to willingly choose to, and accept personal responsibility for their choices <i>because it was actually their choice!</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I prefer that ChroD protagonists be, on some level, broken people and monsters. Vampire wouldn't be anywhere near as interesting if there was no Beast and no need to drink blood, because then you'd just be a superhero. Someone on the forum actually has a signature that even says something like &quot;is it better to be born good or to overcome one's evil nature?&quot; or something like that. My preferences regarding Mage are things that I think the game should have done in the first place, for the reasons I've explained. If you like Mage completely as it is, I'm sorry, but I guess we just aren't going to see eye to eye. </div> </div> </div> I would say that Mage represents the opposite of that quote. &quot;Is it worse to be born evil, or to willing choose to succumb to the temptation to do evil?&quot; I would say that it's the 2nd that Mage chose to cater to and that it is indeed the more sinister option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I've said, I dislike the &quot;they're monsters because they could do bad things with their powers&quot; trope. You can disagree, but no matter how many times you repeat it it won't win me over.<br /> <br /> In a desperate attempt to get us back on topic, does the character concept I proposed go against the nature of the game or setting in any way? </div> </div> </div>You don't need to like it, but you must accept that that is what Mage is based off of, and any attempt you make at changing that will mean changing the nature of the game so completely that you may as well call it a different game at that point.<br /> <br /> Though getting back on topic, no, there's nothing wrong with clockwork mages. You could choose to take dots in Mind to increase your intelligence, crafting, and science scores through the roof to be able to make actual non-magical clockwork creations. You can take Matter and use it to make golems made from clockwork parts, etc., etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:16:23-07:00","id":980520,"title":"","content":"Thanks. We should probably move this to the thread for the Mage hack, since we're off just a specific character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:31:14-07:00","id":980527,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Onyx Path does such good work I'd be pretty much up for anything they made, hence why I'm really looking forward to pugmire. That said, I generally don't really <i>like</i> the superhero genre myself. So while I'm sure they'd be able to make a pretty good one with the people they have writing for them, I can't really vouch much for personal interest.<br /> <br /> Mages get powerful faster by doing terrible things. That's also another part of a Mage ST's job. The path to unraveling the Mystery of a Mages Obsessions don't need to be good. If the only lead they have into progressing their understanding is the read the thoughts of, or mind control helpless sleepers so be it. Might not seem that bad at first, but that's why you steadily lead them deeper and deeper into depravity, step by morally questionable step.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:38:17-07:00","id":980531,"title":"","content":"if you want rules for automatons what about the hedgespun automaton rules in changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:43:52-07:00","id":980535,"title":"","content":"Again, I think we're working on different expectations. The fact that mages can become monstrous isn't enough for me, because ChroD, to me, has been about exploring specific horror archetypes. Mages as they are presented do not much resemble a recognizable monster archetype. Also, everything you've said about what makes mages monstrous fits mad scientists as well or better. It's one of those things that's both counter to my personal preferences and something I consider a genuine flaw.<br /> <br /> And to answer the second, doesn't Mage already have rules for automatons created using magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:53:10-07:00","id":980559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980535#post980535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I think we're working on different expectations. The fact that mages can become monstrous isn't enough for me, because ChroD, to me, has been about exploring specific horror archetypes. Mages as they are presented do not much resemble a recognizable monster archetype. Also, everything you've said about what makes mages monstrous fits mad scientists as well or better. It's one of those things that's both counter to my personal preferences and something I consider a genuine flaw.<br /> <br /> And to answer the second, doesn't Mage already have rules for automatons created using magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more that you seem to like the idea of mad scientists more in general than that it is something that inherently fits them better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:59:54-07:00","id":980563,"title":"","content":"Why not just write Genius 2ed, probably a lot easier then overhauling mage to fit your whims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:02:04-07:00","id":980564,"title":"","content":"A little off topic, why do you say that you need matter + life for an automata? What does Life do?<br /> Wouldnt Matter + Mind or even just Mind be enough to make a &quot;doll&quot; move?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:56:13-07:00","id":980613,"title":"","content":"I'd heard Matter + Life, but I agree that Matter + Mind is probably all you'd need. Maybe you'd need Matter and Life if you wanted to truly create a &quot;living&quot; mechanical creature, but Mind and Matter seems like enough to create a robot. Life + Matter would be to make a prosthetic, but just Matter would probably be enough to create a quick and dirty one. You'd probably need Life to be able to directly hook it to your brain and nervous system, though. Just Matter is enough to form an arm out of stone, but you'd need Mind to make the arm move on its own and Life to functionally connect it to someone. <br /> <br /> You know, that's actually completely on topic, it's all of the last few pages that have been off topic. Thank you for bringing us back around. And the reason I'm not making an entirely new game or Genius 2e is that it's actually less work to hack Mage, and then I can still use all the material OP has published. And I've explained why I think mad scientists are better for modern personal horror than mages. Again- who's the narrator of The Monster Mash? It's not a wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-03-2016, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:45:26-07:00","id":980633,"title":"","content":"I think that all you need is Matter spell. Remember, in 2E you have <i>Remote Control</i> spell on Matter 1 and with 1 Reach you can make complex operations with it. Just cast it on you prosthesis arm with this Reach and Indefinite, and you literally has arm that works under your will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:22:37-07:00","id":980978,"title":"","content":"Hm, though, I don't think that would enable you to feel things with the arm, and that's probably something a lot of people would value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:18:19-07:00","id":981017,"title":"","content":"To 'feel' a things through the arm you just give extra Mind 1 or Life 1 component, i.e. Knowing spells. Voila, you have magically build arm that feels as real one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:28:59-07:00","id":981158,"title":"","content":"Yeah. That's what I was saying, you'd need another Arcana to make it feel. Didn't know you could do it with Mind, though.<br /> <br /> Technically, you could also make automatons with Prime, Death, or Spirit by binding stuff to your machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:16:05-07:00","id":981335,"title":"","content":"Theoretically, you could also make prosthetics with Forces by manipulating kinetic energy or Space by creating hard boundaries. I'd argue you could also do it with Fate and Time, but since Ananke are a feat of archmastery it might not be worth the trouble. Really, there's probably a way with any arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:43:40-07:00","id":981465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977718-clockwork-mage-build-advice?p=980535#post980535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to answer the second, doesn't Mage already have rules for automatons created using magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not sure if this is a rhetorical question, but ill answer anyway.<br /> In Mage Tome of the Mysteries there are rules to make golems. Just resking them as clockwork machines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}